   "result": "The held-out set does not overturn the dev-set decision, but it sharpens the cost. On the shipped operators and scoring, 12 of 30 real commits are REJECTED on their own tests alone (18/30 accepted). Removing the integer +-1 mutants accepts 24/30, and so does per-line scoring under the expressions policy. Neither the commits nor the rejections are labelled: nothing here separates a rejection that catches weak tests from a false one. So the measured fact is a 40% fail-closed rate on agent-authored work, not a 40% false-rejection rate. A rejection routes the order to a founder acceptance test (the oracle path), so the cost is founder attention, not a wrong acceptance. The next decisive evidence is a labelled corpus, mainly wrong changes that these tests pass.",
